# v1.0.4

## English

### Highlights

- **wayshot-cli** — New headless command-line tool covering screenshot, screen recording, video, audio, editing and AI capabilities, designed for LLM / script invocation (no GUI required).
- **Slint 1.19** — Upgraded from 1.17.1 to 1.19 with edition 1.19 compilation; dynamic z-ordering is now built into Slint, so the bundled 1.17 vendor patch is gone.
- **Subtitle Outline Rework** — Subtitle strokes now use a Euclidean distance-transform dilation, removing the fuzz around curved glyph edges.
- **Dependency Modernization** — webrtc/rtc 0.21, burn 0.22 (CPU backend moved to `flex`), ashpd 0.14, speakrs, opus 0.4, silero 0.7, minijinja 3, eframe 0.37.

### Features

#### wayshot-cli
- Covers capture, camera, audio, video, project editing, image ops, AI tools (OCR, erase, code image, LLM, TTS, music), danmaku, dedup, similar-video search and downloads
- Own workspace member with its own `Cargo.lock`, usable independently of the GUI

#### Timeline & Editing
- Subtitle outline via distance-field dilation (`draw-utils` gains Euclidean distance transform + stroke mask generation, with a rendering verification example)
- Merging subtitle segments with the previous one no longer inserts a redundant space after Chinese punctuation
- Added a `subtitle_outline_demo` example to verify stroke quality

#### Packaging & Build
- New Arch Linux packaging script (`packing-archlinux.sh`)
- New `make install-linx` target: release build installed to `~/.local/bin`, previous binary backed up as `.bak`

### Improvements

- **Slint 1.19 migration**: 332 default-valued property bindings removed; `DesktopPanel` / `LandingPage` now follow the window size explicitly, fixing the collapsed main body and the width binding loops in the filter panel and the four preview containers
- Dialog callbacks unified to `close` / `canceled` / `confirmed`; deprecated `viewport-*` properties migrated to `content-*`
- `const-field-offset` bumped to 0.2.1 to fix a `compose_field_offsets` compilation failure in the 1.18 generated code
- Project path/name resolution unified via `project_path_with_ext` and `project_name_from_path`; MCP-created projects now sync their name to the window title, backup directories only strip the `.wayshot` suffix
- ashpd 0.14 adaptation for screencast `SourceType` / `CursorMode` constants
- burn 0.22: `voxcpm-rs` migrated to the backend-free generic API, weight dtype derived from the device, pth loading moved to the new `pytorch-reader` interface; GPU cleanup goes through `Device::sync` / `memory_cleanup`
- webrtc 0.21: `SettingEngineBuilder`, fully-populated `Sample`, non-exhaustive `TrackLocalEvent`; WHEP client gains a `PeerConnectionEventHandler`, payload-type negotiation and RTCP feedback draining
- Removed the `bincode` dependency; `vendor/speakrs` and its `[patch.crates-io]` entry dropped now that upstream covers it
- GitHub Actions toolchain upgraded; `.mcp.json` removed; rustfmt unified across `wayshot/src` and examples

### Bug Fixes

- **Project names containing dots**: extension was not appended and the name got truncated, producing a wrong window title
- **Preview player after seek**: the player was overwritten into a paused state; `seek` no longer touches `is_previewing` and restores playback based on the outcome
- **Subtitle export**: SRT numbering started at 0; exporting a single subtitle no longer puts the track index into the filename
- **Subtitle merge**: following segments were incorrectly shifted by the gap duration after merging
- **Subtitle style**: font style was not synced when extracting styles; switching text elements left stale input content
- MusicGen and preference settings dialog layouts fixed; export panel subtitle format radios laid out horizontally
- Stale interface calls in the `stem-splitter` and `dewatermark` examples fixed

